From 4f776a1ba58a10e607224005cedf1a7a94c4db8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 12:39:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix MCP OAuth auto-discovery and auto-connect-on-add

- tools/mcp_oauth.py: fix a typo'd `import httpx2` (nonexistent package,
  not in requirements.txt) that was silently caught by the module's own
  `except ImportError: HAS_OAUTH = False` guard. This made the entire
  OAuth auto-detection/discovery/DCR flow a permanent no-op regardless of
  what the target MCP server supported -- oauth_enabled() always returned
  False and probe_oauth() always returned None. Renamed all httpx2 refs to
  httpx (the actual installed dependency).

- dawn-ui/src/app/mcp/page.tsx: even with detection fixed, OAuth was only
  ever probed reactively after a failed manual 'Connect' click, and even
  then just showed a 'Sign in' button the user had to notice and click.
  Now:
    * handleAdd immediately attempts to connect right after creating the
      server, instead of just saving the row and stopping.
    * handleConnect auto-invokes handleSignIn (which opens the consent
      popup and retries connect on completion) the moment a 401 is
      detected as OAuth, instead of waiting for a separate click.
  Together this makes add -> probe -> auto-launch-consent behave like
  Claude's own connector flow.

- dawn-api/tests/test_mcp_oauth_import.py: regression test asserting
  HAS_OAUTH is True, no httpx2 references remain, and probe_oauth actually
  reaches httpx.AsyncClient.post. Verified this fails (2/3 cases) against
  the pre-fix code and passes against the fix.
